    branch    next
    commit    63f2b66ddc48f0d66574d2e9c2076dbf60fb8fb5
    date      2026-08-11

No `upstream` remote is configured, and upstream releases are not merged. The fork is taken
over rather than tracked. `tools/rename.mjs` is retained as a record of how the namespace was
applied, not as a live tool.

Modifications
-------------

The Web Awesome namespace has been renamed throughout: `wa-` element, class, cascade-layer and
event names to `cs-`; `--wa-` custom properties to `--cs-`; exported `Wa*` classes to `Cs*`; and
the package to `@cruglobal/cornerstone-components`. Further changes are recorded in the git
history of the `cornerstone` branch.

Excluded from this fork
-----------------------

Web Awesome Pro is not part of the upstream public repository and is not included here. Font
Awesome icon assets carry licensing separate from the Web Awesome source and are not vendored.
Upstream documentation prose IS carried over. The documentation site was ported from upstream's
`docs/` tree with the namespace rename applied and has been edited since; measured against the fork
point, 72% of its substantial prose lines are still upstream's verbatim. It is covered by the same MIT
licence and the attribution above.

Inherited test failures
-----------------------

Eight tests failed on the unmodified upstream tree at the fork point, in WebKit and Firefox. They
were recorded in `tools/baseline-failures.txt` so that later failures could be told apart from
inherited ones. All eight are resolved — fixed, or skipped with the reason recorded in the test —
and the suite is green on Chromium, Firefox and WebKit. That file was deleted on 2026-08-17, its
job done.
